 "notes": "Stretch 3. p. 110 all rows; p. 111 rows 1-6 only, stopping at the rule above '1. Re en tem erṭāt śāṭ tep se' (next part, not read). No footnotes on pp. 110-111 in this stretch. Line numerals: line 3 in force at the top of p. 110 (3. printed on p. 109 last row). 4. p. 110 row 2 before śāṭ; 5. p. 110 row 3 inside remu (between G43 and the fish K1) - remu kept in line 4, the following em is line 5; 6. p. 110 row 7 (third row under 'ki re') at its start before ennuḥti; 7. p. 110 row 8 inside àstu - à (before A1) - word kept in 6; 8. p. 110 row 9 inside ṭeb - k (after D46) - word kept in 7; 9. p. 111 row 2 inside ḥetem - f (after V28 + second sign) - word kept in 8; 10. p. 111 row 3 inside àm - à (before A1) - word kept in 9. XCIII A ('ki re', Another chapter) does not restart numbering: the heading and the first row under it are line 5. Rubric: only the centred heading 'ki re' has an overline (over both groups); no other overlines in the stretch. p. 110 row 3: Budge prints a dotted lacuna '...........' in the English under χer - k (after 'Not' under àn), and '[—]' (bracketed flat sign) before the owl of ām in the hieroglyph line: ām marked restored. Other hieroglyph brackets: us[eb] (D58) p. 110 row 9; àm - [à] (A1) p. 111 row 4. Brackets only in transliteration/English: ī - ku[à] (p. 110 row 8, no sign printed for à), '[hostile]' and '[shall be done to me]' in English. Glosses spanning two words given on the first (ka+eref 'in very truth'; ḥetep+neter 'of the divine offerings'). The negative àn printed sometimes with N35 below, sometimes alone - coded as printed."
